<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 14-AUG.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 14-AUG.</headline>
<text>
<p>Supertyphoon Winnie is now about 450 miles west of the Mariana Islands and moving to the northwest. Top winds are 155 mph and are forecast to slowly weaken. The storm will be monitored for future impact on eastern Asia.  </p>
<p>Heavy thunderstorms caused major flash flooding near Hong Kong during the past 36 hours. Additional storms may occur off and on during the next few days.  </p>
<p>Nothing further at this time.</p>
</text>
